# Into the Mists: the arrival on the Old Svalich Road (docs/regions/into_the_mists.md).
# Started by props on into_the_mists_road: mists_wall (the fog at the east edge), mists_deer_carcass and
# edge_alley_crow (Speak with Animals: Rose and Thorn have no smell; the pack under the carcass).

~ mist_wall
narrate examine:mists_wall
if not flag.mists_arrived
  set mists_arrived
  quest into_the_mists lost_in_mist
  -> hooks
endif
Narrator: You walk into the white, and a dozen steps later you walk out of it facing the same road in the same direction. The mist is not a wall; it is a hand, turning you around.
-> END

# Nothing made the party look back at the mist, so the arrival (and every personal quest with it) could be missed:
# the wolf in the narrows plays it, then the standoff goes on, if it hasn't played (Wiki finding 2).
~ first_sight
set mists_arrived
set mists_arrival_late
quest into_the_mists lost_in_mist
-> hooks

~ hooks
cutscene mists_arrival
Narrator: Each of you came looking for something. None of you came looking for this.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: A land of mists. This is it. Sir Pellam, I'm here. I've got your sword. I've not dropped it once. Well. Once.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: A valley in a ring of mountains, and no sun. I've seen this sky before. I saw it on the morning of my vows.
interject name:thistle: Grandda's blazes came this way. Right into the fog. He went in here. So I'm going in here.
interject name:ratatoille: Somewhere in this fog is the Wizard of Wines. A master of the arcane and the table. He's going to be so impressed with me.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: "The valley where the sun does not rise." Well, he wasn't wrong. Hello, Kasimir, wherever you are. Got post for you.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: A land of mists. Right. Lord of a land of mists. One signature. That's all. How hard can one signature be?
# Each pregen's personal quest starts here (docs/story/personal_quests.md); a custom hero in their place starts none.
if name:godrick_pendlebrook
quest the_ladle the_errand
endif
if name:liriel_dawnsong
quest carry_the_dawn the_vision
endif
if name:thistle
quest fens_trail the_trail
endif
if name:ratatoille
quest a_seat_at_the_table the_apprenticeship
endif
if name:wren_featherfoot
quest the_last_lesson the_letter
endif
if name:kip_smudgewick
quest the_fine_print the_contract
endif
# The first four (kept for older saves).
if name:ilse_varga
quest kestrel_company the_letter
endif
if name:tamsin_tealeaf
quest the_locket the_dreams
endif
if name:hedda_ironvow
quest cold_prayers the_dream
endif
if name:silvain_aster
quest aurels_last_chapter the_letter
endif
if not name:godrick_pendlebrook
  interject class:fighter: Road goes one way. So do we.
endif
if not name:liriel_dawnsong
  interject class:cleric: Whatever brought us here went to some trouble. That's worth remembering.
endif
if flag.mists_arrival_late and not flag.mists_wolves_resolved
-> into_the_mists/wolves:nerves
endif
* Try walking back into the mist. -> again
* Follow the road. -> END

~ again
Narrator: The mist lets you in, holds you a moment like a host taking your coat, and hands you back to the road, facing west.
interject name:ratatoille: Not an illusion. Illusions have a smell, like burnt sugar. This smells of nothing at all. I like that a great deal less.
if not name:ratatoille
  interject class:wizard: That isn't fog. That's a border, and it has opinions.
endif
-> END

~ carcass
narrate examine:mists_deer_carcass
if flag.mists_read_the_pack
  Narrator: The kill is still here, still uneaten. The wolves that left it are still somewhere ahead.
  -> END
endif
if flag.mists_carcass_studied
  Narrator: The ground has told you all it's going to.
  -> END
endif
* [Survival DC 12] Read the tracks around it. -> carcass_tracks | carcass_no_tracks
* Leave it. -> END

~ carcass_tracks
set mists_carcass_studied
set mists_read_the_pack
Narrator: {name} reads the churned earth: a dozen wolves moving in a line, not a scatter, and a kill they never touched. They were not hungry; they were busy.
interject name:thistle: That's not a hunt. Wolves in a line like that, somebody's walking them. Like dogs.
if not name:thistle
  interject background:soldier: Wolves in a line. That's a picket. Somebody gives them orders.
endif
-> END

~ carcass_no_tracks
set mists_carcass_studied
Narrator: Prints, fog and old leaves, churned into one dark mess by something large, numerous and gone. Probably gone.
-> END

# --- The crow on a barrel at the village edge (prop edge_alley_crow) ---

~ crow
narrate examine:edge_alley_crow
* [if spell:speak_with_animals] Ask the crow what it's seen. -> crow_speaks
* [if not spell:speak_with_animals] [knows:speak_with_animals] (Cast Speak with Animals, and ask the crow what it's seen.) -> crow_cast
* [if spell:speak_with_animals or knows:speak_with_animals] Leave it to its barrel. -> END
-> END

~ crow_cast
cast speak_with_animals
if check.last
-> crow_speaks
endif
-> END

~ crow_speaks
set mists_crow_told
Narrator: The crow puts its head on one side and talks fast, in clicks and little pictures, like a gossip who has waited all morning for someone to tell.
Narrator: "The two small ones in the road have no smell. None. Not boy, not girl, not even scared. They smell like the white. The tall house eats the ones who go in. Crows don't sit on its roof."
Narrator: "Back up the road, under the dead deer, there's a man-bag the wolves didn't want. Buckles. Too heavy for me. You can have it."
reveal carcass_pack
-> END
